+# Secrets for bin/kamal. Kamal reads this file on your machine and passes the
+# listed values to the container. This file holds no values, only references to
+# environment variables, so it is safe to commit.
+#
+# Export the values before you run bin/kamal. Keep them in your password manager.
+#
+#   SECRET_KEY_BASE   Create once with `bin/rails secret`. Keep it stable: changing
+#                     it signs every user out.
+#   SMTP_PASSWORD     Your SMTP password. Leave it empty if the server needs no login.
+#   VAPID_*           Web push keys, optional. Create a pair with:
+#                     bin/rails runner 'k = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{k.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{k.private_key}"'
+
+SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
+SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
+VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
